messages.body_plain:
Hi Richard,

- Indent the program in a sensible way. It's really hard to track through what's going on without that. (I use the stan emacs mode, which handles consistent indentation.)
- Create a generated quantities block. Move the calculation of covmat to generated quantities since you're not using it anywhere in the model block. Follow Bob's advice on using quad_form_diag().
- Data: add constraints to your data. I think this model might not work as you intended since Y_treatment is a vector and not an integer array. In the model block, there's an "if (Y_treatment[i] == 1)". If Y_treatment[i] isn't exactly 1, your model may not behave as you intended.
- Calculate log(sigma1) and log(sigma2) outside the for loop.
- Any reason you've parameterized Lambda as a corr_matrix[3] instead of just dealing with two correlation parameters directly (Lambda[1,2] and Lambda[1,3])? I think that would help the model, but I'm not sure.

Daniel

